  "caption": "Quinn started a retail job: on the feet all day. By hour seven the legs felt like concrete.\n\nStanding still can be harder on the body than moving. Muscles stay switched on and fluid can pool in the lower legs, so ten static hours is its own kind of overload.\n\nWhat can help: shifting weight often and resting one foot on a low rail, calf raises every hour, supportive shoes replaced regularly, plus anti-fatigue mats and compression socks (check with your GP first if you have circulation issues or diabetes).\n\nGet it checked if one calf is swollen, warm or sore, the skin over veins changes, or you notice morning heel pain, numbness or back pain down a leg.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
